  "published": "2026-10-01T10:40:50.55Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.0: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.5.0 (Task-based API; see its notes)\n\nv0.4.16: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.16\n- CHANGED: Braket results carry their recorded counts, so measuring a returned state yields Braket's own shots rather than outcomes resampled from its amplitudes\n\nv0.4.14: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.14\n- ADDED: the Braket backend implements IShotSamplingBackend, so sampled UCCSD-VQE knows its shot count\n- CHANGED: circuits are transpiled to the target device's gate set before OpenQASM 3.0 export, so composite gates (Toffoli, multi-controlled, controlled-phase) reach the device; an optional JobBudget limits submitted jobs\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.14+",
